{
  "name": "Saltmarsh",
  "tagline": "Estuary colours: sea lavender, cordgrass, samphire, tide",
  "story": "Saltmarsh is the edge of an estuary at low tide: sea lavender in flower, cordgrass gone to straw, samphire reddening on the mud, and the channel water holding the sky. Keywords take the lavender, strings the straw, numbers the samphire, types the tide water. Grounds are muted fog, channel slate or dusk brown, never pure black or white, and every syntax colour clears WCAG AA against them, so long sessions stay low-glare.",
